    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.Heading">HandleScope integration</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.Detail">Install, verify, and connect SessionDock to the optional local HandleScope API.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.CheckingSetup">Checking local setup...</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.CheckingDetail">SessionDock is inspecting local files only.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.Attention">Configuration needs attention</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.AttentionDetail">SessionDock preserved the existing configuration and will not use it. Repair replaces only the SessionDock opt-in with the fixed, minimal Roblox policy; it does not install, start, or stop HandleScope.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.Controls">CONNECTION AND CONTROLS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.SecurityDetail">The install button downloads only the pinned official HandleScope v0.1.4 Windows x64 package. SessionDock verifies its fixed size and SHA-256 hash, the matching checksum, safe ZIP layout, and internal file inventory before running the standard-user installer. The verified child process uses RemoteSigned so Windows’ default Restricted policy does not reject it; Bypass and Unrestricted are never used, saved policy is unchanged, and Group Policy remains authoritative. Installation starts the API and enables its limited per-user autostart; enabling the SessionDock integration remains a separate explicit choice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.InstallTooltip">Download, verify, and install the pinned HandleScope v0.1.4 release for this Windows user</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.InstallName">Install HandleScope v0.1.4</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.Install">Install HandleScope v0.1.4</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.InstallConfirm">SessionDock will download the pinned HandleScope v0.1.4 Windows x64 package from the canonical Makmatoe/HandleScope GitHub release. Before anything runs, it verifies the fixed package size and SHA-256 hash, the matching same-release checksum, safe ZIP layout, and every file in the internal inventory. If an older supported per-user installation is present, this action may replace it.&#10;&#10;HandleScope is not Authenticode-signed. These checks confirm the reviewed immutable GitHub release rather than a certificate-backed publisher. The standard-user installer starts the API now and enables its limited autostart at Windows sign-in. The verified child process uses RemoteSigned so Windows’ default Restricted policy does not reject it; SessionDock never uses Bypass or Unrestricted, changes saved policy, overrides Group Policy, elevates, or enables the integration automatically.&#10;&#10;Continue?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.InstallConfirmTitle">Install HandleScope v0.1.4</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.InstallSucceeded">HandleScope {0} was verified and installed. Its API was started and limited per-user autostart was enabled. Select Enable to opt SessionDock in.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.InstallCanceled">HandleScope installation was canceled before the installer started.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.InstallFailed">HandleScope could not be installed safely. No unverified package was run.&#10;&#10;Reason: {0}&#10;&#10;Check the official setup guide: {1}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.InstallFailureDownload">GitHub could not provide the pinned HandleScope release. Check the network connection and try again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.InstallFailureIntegrity">The download did not match the pinned size, SHA-256, checksum, redirect, ZIP, or internal inventory checks. Do not run it manually.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.InstallFailureEnvironment">Windows could not prepare the verified installer safely. Run SessionDock as a standard user and check the temporary folder and local security controls.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Handle.InstallFailureInstaller">The verified HandleScope installer was refused or could not finish. Refresh the integration status before retrying because files may already have been installed. If PowerShell Group Policy blocks it, use the official guide or contact the administrator.</sys:String>
