    <sys:String x:Key="LinkIntegration.Title">Open with SessionDock</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LinkIntegration.Heading">Open with SessionDock</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LinkIntegration.Detail">An optional per-user Windows handler for Roblox links. SessionDock always shows a preview and account chooser; receiving a link never launches Roblox by itself.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LinkIntegration.Checking">Checking Windows registration...</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LinkIntegration.ChangesHeading">What enabling changes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LinkIntegration.ChangesDetail">SessionDock adds only keys for this Windows user under HKCU\Software\Classes: its owned URL handler, its private sessiondock-roblox: protocol, and an Open With hint for roblox: links. It does not replace Roblox's default handler, register for all web links, elevate, or send data online.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LinkIntegration.SafetyHeading">Safety at launch</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LinkIntegration.SafetyDetail">Only official roblox.com HTTPS links and restricted roblox: links are accepted. Authentication tickets, cookies, tokens, JobIds, unknown parameters, and non-Roblox links are refused. Private-server codes are hidden in the preview and are not saved to account defaults or history.</sys:String>
